# TEMPLATE-llamacpp — a Mac or Windows variant, served by llama.cpp.
#
# The same eight questions as TEMPLATE.env, answered for llama.cpp: one GGUF
# file, the llama.cpp build rack pins (Metal on a Mac, CUDA on Windows through
# WSL2), kept alive by launchd or a systemd user unit. `rack new <name>
# <org/model> --mac` (or --windows) writes model.env and copies this file from
# the "# --- 1 FIT" line down into <name>/mac.env.


# --- 1 FIT ------------------------------------------------------------------
# A Mac lets the GPU wire about two thirds of its memory up to 36 GB, three
# quarters above (rack platform prints this machine's number). Windows: the
# GPU's own memory. The GGUF file plus the KV cache must fit in it.
#     rack fit <org/model> --mac
#   file       ___ GB  (quant ___)
#   verdict    ___
WEIGHTS_GB=                     # the GGUF file, in GB

# --- 2 ENGINE ---------------------------------------------------------------
# llama.cpp at rack's pinned build. Does that build know this architecture?
# The GGUF repo's card says which llama.cpp it needs.
ENGINE=llamacpp

# --- 3 ACCESS ---------------------------------------------------------------
# One GGUF file, as <org>/<repo>/<file>.gguf. Q4_K_M on a 16 GB machine,
# Q8_0 where memory allows. Pin the revision you tested.
. "$RECIPE_DIR/model.env"
ARTIFACT=FILL_ME
# ARTIFACT_REVISION=            the repo commit you tested
# ARTIFACT_MMPROJ=              a vision model's projector: <org>/<repo>/<file>.gguf

# --- 4 SHAPE ----------------------------------------------------------------
# rack up sets --host, --port, --alias and --api-key-file.
SERVE_ARGS=(
  --n-gpu-layers 999            # every layer on the GPU
  --ctx-size FILL_ME            # the KV cache grows with this, in the same memory as the weights
  # --parallel 1                # concurrent requests; they share --ctx-size
  # --flash-attn on             # less memory at long context
  # --cache-type-k q8_0 --cache-type-v q8_0   # half the KV memory (with --flash-attn)

  # --- 5 DIALECT ------------------------------------------------------------
  --jinja                       # the model's own chat template: tool calls work
  # --reasoning-format deepseek # thinking goes to reasoning_content, not content
)

# --- 6 ENV ------------------------------------------------------------------
ENV_EXTRA=()

# --- 7 PATCH ----------------------------------------------------------------
# llama.cpp takes no mods: a fix arrives as a newer pinned build.

# --- 8 PROOF ----------------------------------------------------------------
#     rack up <name> --mac && rack bench <label>
#   decode      ___ tok/s
#   TTFT        ___ ms
#   memory      ___ GB          (Activity Monitor's GPU memory, or nvidia-smi)
